+# T00 — Repository Baseline Inventory And Protected-Data Record
+
+Status: **complete for the parts that can be observed in this checkout.**
+Owner: safety/tooling agent. Ticket: [#33](https://github.com/Piskriek/HeavyMetal2/issues/33).
+
+This document records what actually exists in the repository and where the protected
+data stands. Every hash, count and exit code below came from a command that was run in
+this checkout on 2026-09-22; nothing here is estimated or synthesised. The raw baseline
+run log is in [`BASELINE_VERIFICATION.md`](./BASELINE_VERIFICATION.md).
+
+---
+
+## 1. What was inventoried (and how)
+
+| Area | Command used | Result |
+| :--- | :--- | :--- |
+| Revision | `git log --oneline -5`, `git status --porcelain` | `08ebf4d` "dont need" is the only commit; this branch adds `94dc206` (tooling only) |
+| Toolchain | `node --version`, `npm --version` | Node v22.22.3, npm 10.9.8 |
+| Lockfile | `node -e` over `package-lock.json` | lockfileVersion 3, 224 packages, all with `integrity` + `resolved` |
+| Install | `npm ci --no-audit --no-fund` | 131 packages added, exit 0 |
+| Sources | `find src -type f`, `wc -l` | 67 files, 17,222 lines TS/TSX, 1,707 lines CSS |
+| Scripts | `ls scripts/`, header comments, `grep -n writeFileSync` | 31 `.mjs` scripts (30 pre-existing + the new safeguard) plus `crop_signs.ps1` |
+| Tests | `ls tests/`, header comments | 12 suites at `08ebf4d` (6 unit `*.test.ts`, 6 browser `*.mjs`); this branch adds a 13th, `tests/protect-baseline.test.ts` |
+| Storage writers | `grep -rn "localStorage.setItem" src`, `vite.config.ts` | see §4 |
+| Protected data | `node scripts/protect-baseline.mjs inventory` | see §3 |
+
+### 1.1 Engine, renderer, builder (sizes in lines)
+
+| File | Lines | Role |
+| :--- | ---: | :--- |
+| `src/game/track-builder-3d.ts` | 2,350 | Authoring surface: prop placement, undo/redo, `saveToStorage()`, `/api/backup-props` calls |
+| `src/components/TrackBuilderUI.tsx` | 2,307 | Builder UI, backup/restore modal, disk-backup list |
+| `src/game/renderer-3d.ts` | 1,897 | three.js rendering. Constructs `new THREE.WebGLRenderer` at line 1657 — **the app cannot render a race without WebGL** |
+| `src/game/environment.ts` | 1,122 | Sky/backdrop/ambient layers |
+| `src/game/engine.ts` | 1,013 | Fixed-step simulation |
+| `src/game/save.ts` | 500 | Versioned session save (`goblin-rally-session-v1`) with a backup key |
+| `src/game/scene.ts` / `projection.ts` / `geometry.ts` | 244 / 344 / 308 | Geometry, camera and track-space math |
+| `src/game/session.ts`, `preferences.ts`, `controls.ts` | 143 / 68 / 216 | Event setup, user options/records, key bindings |
+
+### 1.2 Scripts (audited before execution)
+
+None of the pre-existing scripts write into `backups/props/**`; only `vite.config.ts`
+(dev server) does that. Classification:
+
+| Category | Scripts | Writes to |
+| :--- | :--- | :--- |
+| Verification (read-only) | `check.mjs`, `check-edge-magenta.mjs`, `browser-check.mjs`, `protect-baseline.mjs`, `probe-webgl.mjs` | `tests/artifacts/**` only |
+| Generators | `build-art.mjs`, `generate-stylized-track-textures.mjs`, `generate-bandaid-decals.mjs`, `generate-warcraft-fringe.mjs`, `cut-ui-art.mjs`, `make-skybox-seamless.mjs`, `process-*.mjs`, `color-match-textures.mjs`, `balance-asset-color.mjs`, `scan-magenta.mjs` | `public/**`, `src/game/art-manifest.json`, `tests/artifacts/**` |
+| Repair | `fix-edge-magenta.mjs`, `edge-magenta-lib.mjs` | rewrites runtime PNGs — deliberately **not** run |
+| **Windows-only (13)** | `capture-stages.mjs`, `clean-all-magenta-bleed.mjs`, `clean-pines.mjs`, `inspect-pines.mjs`, `key-crowd.mjs`, `optimize-assets.mjs`, `process-blizzard-decals.mjs`, `process-modular-archway.mjs`, `process-start-archway.mjs`, `process-treewalls.mjs`, `process-warcraft-decals.mjs`, `run-preview-screenshots.mjs`, `test-despill.mjs` | hard-code `C:\Program Files (x86)\Microsoft\Edge\Application\msedge.exe`; cannot run on this Linux checkout |
+
+`npm run fix:edges`, `art:textures`, `balance:art` and `seamless:sky` rewrite art and were
+not executed: T00 is a baseline ticket and must not change protected or generated bytes.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Where the game persists data (§1 storage writers)
+
+| Store | Key / path | Written by |
+| :--- | :--- | :--- |
+| Decoration working copy | `localStorage['hm2-3d-track-props']` | `track-builder-3d.ts:2091` |
+| Decoration in-browser backup | `localStorage['hm2-3d-track-props-backup-latest']` | `track-builder-3d.ts:2099` |
+| Decoration in-browser history (5) | `localStorage['hm2-3d-track-props-backup-history']` | `track-builder-3d.ts:2112` |
+| Builder defaults | `hm2-3d-track-sky`, `hm2-builder-camera-facing-default`, `hm2-builder-decal-default`, `hm2-builder-decal-lighting-default` | `track-builder-3d.ts:429-538` |
+| Event/session | `goblin-rally-session-v1` (+ `-backup`) | `save.ts` |
+| Setup, options, records, bindings | `goblin-rally-setup-v2`, `goblin-rally-options-v1`, `goblin-rally-records-v1`, `goblin-rally-keybindings-v1` | `session.ts`, `preferences.ts`, `controls.ts` |
+| **Disk mirror of decorations** | `backups/props/track-props-latest.json` | dev server `POST /api/backup-props` (`vite.config.ts`) |
+| Disk history (pruned to 30) | `backups/props/history/props-<course>-<ts>.json` | same endpoint |
+| Starter preset (shipped) | `public/presets/track-props-default.json` | committed asset |
+
+The dev-server endpoint refuses to overwrite a non-empty baseline with an empty array
+and prunes history to 30 files; `POST /api/restore-backup` resolves `path.basename(...)`
+only. Any future ticket that adds a writer must not target the protected path (T08).
+
+---
+
+## 3. Protected data: what exists, and the explicit blocker
+
+**The protected file is the user-authored 3D decoration baseline** — the prop set the
+Track Builder produces. Its authoritative copy lives in the user's browser
+(`localStorage['hm2-3d-track-props']`) and is mirrored to disk by the dev server.
+
+`npm run inventory:baseline` (read-only) reported on 2026-09-22. It prints
+`AUTHORISED BASELINE: <snapshot dir>` when a verified snapshot of these exact bytes exists
+and `BLOCKER: no authorised snapshot …` when it does not — the status is derived from a
+manifest, never assumed:
+
+| Role | Path | Status | sha256 | Bytes | Observed props |
+| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | ---: | ---: |
+| primary-disk-mirror | `backups/props/track-props-latest.json` | present | `0721aa4b1e0e37f273cf0782fc643ff891455ba6f712c36ea851cd9d4f38a7a5` | 94,867 | 237 (237 unique IDs, 0 duplicates, 0 missing) |
+| starter-preset-mirror | `backups/props/track-props-default.json` | present | `2af500990d6f49f2b08ede18fa1bb32eb2bc9715c97087d29fa0ec84d1d7eadf` | 3,659 | 14 |
+| starter-preset-shipped | `public/presets/track-props-default.json` | present | `2af500990d6f49f2b08ede18fa1bb32eb2bc9715c97087d29fa0ec84d1d7eadf` | 3,659 | 14 |
+
+Recovery candidates found: **37** files under `backups/props/user_safety_backup/` (7) and
+`backups/props/history/` (30). Two of them are byte-identical to the primary:
+
+- `backups/props/user_safety_backup/track-props-237-props-safeguard.json`
+- `backups/props/history/props-ridge-1790060522733.json`
+
+A third, older copy differs deliberately:
+`user_safety_backup/track-props-latest-safeguard.json` — sha256 `6707d9a88d0a9fb450729c6ec559d55d07d86d433807ecf9e3b1e3331610852f`,
+77,979 bytes, 199 props, `updatedAt 2026-09-22T05:02:37.173Z`.
+
+### Resolution: the user authorised the backup on 2026-09-22
+
+The user confirmed the decoration JSON is backed up and authorised a throw-away copy for
+experiments: *"The decorations json file is backed up, use a _tmp version for now if you
+need"*. That resolves the availability blocker. The first certified snapshot was taken
+from that authorised source:
+
+| Snapshot | Value |
+| :--- | :--- |
+| Directory | `baseline/snapshots/track-props-latest-2026-09-22T13-38-44-625Z/` |
+| Source bytes | `backups/props/track-props-latest.json`, sha256 `0721aa4b1e0e37f273cf0782fc643ff891455ba6f712c36ea851cd9d4f38a7a5`, 94,867 bytes |
+| Read-back | byte-for-byte match against the source |
+| Recovery copy 1 | `backups/props/user_safety_backup/track-props-237-props-safeguard.json` → match |
+| Recovery copy 2 | `backups/props/history/props-ridge-1790060522733.json` → match |
+| Observation | 237 props, 237 unique IDs, 0 duplicates, 45 distinct prop types, course `ridge` |
+
+Reproduce or extend it at any time with:
+
+```bash
+npm run protect:baseline -- --recovery backups/props/user_safety_backup/track-props-237-props-safeguard.json
+npm run verify:baseline
+```
+
+### Remaining limitations (explicit)
+
+- **Single medium.** Both verified copies live on the same disk inside the same checkout.
+  Byte-equality is proven; independence is not. A copy on a second medium remains the
+  user's call and is the only thing that would survive losing this machine.
+- **Disposable copies only.** `tmp-copy` writes to `scratch/` or `tests/artifacts/` (both
+  git-ignored) and refuses every other destination, including `backups/props/**`. A tmp
+  copy is never a baseline and never enters a commit.
+- The hashes above describe the authorised copies. The count (237) and the ID list are
+  **observations**: the manifest marks them `advisory: true` — "never hard-code them as
+  runtime constants" — and the decoration set legitimately changes as the user edits it.
+
+### Usage
+
+```bash
+npm run inventory:baseline                 # read-only status
+npm run protect:baseline                   # exclusive timestamped snapshot + manifest
+npm run protect:baseline -- --recovery backups/props/user_safety_backup/track-props-237-props-safeguard.json
+npm run verify:baseline                    # re-hash newest snapshot, source and recovery copy
+node scripts/protect-baseline.mjs tmp-copy # verified disposable copy at scratch/track-props-latest.tmp.json
+node scripts/protect-baseline.mjs tmp-copy --dest scratch/mine.tmp.json
+```
+
+Snapshots land in `baseline/snapshots/` (new directory) — never inside `backups/props/`.
+The tool refuses escapes, absolute paths, symlinked components and protected-path writes,
+never overwrites, never restores, and exits 1 with a `E_*` code when a check fails.
